        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            There are only four ways a humidifier adds moisture: wick and fan, ultrasonic plate, spinning impeller or boiling. Evaporative is the safest all-rounder, ultrasonic is the quiet choice on soft water, steam gives the cleanest output at the highest power cost, and whole-house units make sense only with forced-air heat.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Choose the mechanism for your water and your room, then the size for your space, and keep the humidity between 30 and 50 percent. Get those right and almost any well-made model will do its job.
          </p>
